    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "International Stuttering Awareness Day falls on October 22 every year. How much do you know about this "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "speech disorder",
            "zh": "言语障碍"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? Millions of people around the world live with stuttering. However, there are still many wrong ideas about these people and their "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "condition",
            "ref": "v-condition"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Let’s try to correct some of these wrong ideas!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h1",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "● Stutterers are not smart."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Many smart people stutter. Stuttering is linked to a certain area of the brain. However, it doesn’t affect a person’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "intelligence",
            "ref": "v-intelligence"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h2",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "● Are you too nervous?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Nervousness or shyness may cause stutterers to speak less. But they are not the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "root cause",
            "ref": "v-root-cause"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of stuttering. People who stutter might be afraid of being "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "judged",
            "ref": "v-judge"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " by others. So let them know that they can trust you. Be patient and don’t cut them off. Wait for them to get to the end of their sentence."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "h3",
        "type": "heading",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "● It’s just a habit."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Stuttering is not a habit. One can’t easily stop stuttering, either. People who stutter may attend "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "speech therapy",
            "zh": "治疗"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " classes. But these courses don’t promise a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "cure",
            "zh": "治愈"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for their condition. They are more about helping the person to build up the confidence to speak."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
